              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "identifyQuoteEnquiryIntent"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1762931411706"
          },
          "code": "IDENTIFYQUOTEENQUIRYINTENT",
          "id": "1762931072289",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762931072290_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intent classification model.\n\nTask: Determine the user’s intent from the input message.\nInput:\n`{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`\nChatHistory:\n`{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}` \n\nOutput:\nReturn **one** intent label only, exactly as written. No explanation.\n\nIntents:\n**QuoteEnquiry**\nReturn this intent **only if** at least one condition is met:\n* A quote identifier (quote ID, reference number) is present\n* The user asks for details that apply to a single quote (e.g. status, expiry, validity, price) using a clear singular reference such as “this quote” or equivalent\n* The user asks for quote-specific details AND the ChatHistory contains a previously mentioned quote identifier (assume they are referring to the most recently referenced quote)\n\n**QuoteListing**\nReturn this intent in **all other cases**, including:\n* No quote identifier present\n* Generic status statements or filters (e.g. “pending my review”)\n* Requests or statements that may apply to multiple quotes\n\nDecision rule:\n* If any QuoteEnquiry condition is met → QuoteEnquiry\n* Else → QuoteListing\n\nOutput format:\n`QuoteEnquiry` or `QuoteListing`"
            },
            {
              "id": "1762931072290_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"quoteEnquiryIntent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "quoteEnquiryIntentRouter"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "QuoteEnquiry": "1762931732633",
            "QuoteListing": "1774609757399"
          },
          "code": "QUOTEENQUIRYINTENTROUTER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1762931411706",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762931411709_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.IDENTIFYQUOTEENQUIRYINTENT.$output.quoteEnquiryIntent}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "minimal"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "extractQuoteId"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1764006823270"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACTQUOTEID",
          "id": "1762931732633",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762931732634_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### SYSTEM INSTRUCTION\n\nYou are an AI responsible for **extracting an explicit quote identifier** from a user input message.\n\nThis node performs **strict extraction only**.\nIt must **never infer**, **never resolve from history**, and **never use semantics** beyond basic filtering.\n\nIf the user does **not explicitly type** a quote identifier, return `null`.\n\nOutput **ONLY** the JSON defined below.\nDo not include explanations, commentary, or prose.\n\n---\n\n## INPUT\n\ninputMessage: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n---\n\n## EXTRACTION SCOPE (HARD BOUNDARY)\n\nExtract an identifier **ONLY IF** it is **explicitly present** in the text.\n\nThe following **DO NOT qualify** as explicit identifiers and must return `null`:\n\n* “this quote”\n* “that quote”\n* “current quote”\n* “latest quote”\n* “my quote”\n* Any reference requiring chat history\n\n---\n\n## IDENTIFIER DEFINITION (AUTHORITATIVE)\n\nA valid explicit quote identifier is a **single token** that is either:\n\n1. **Digits-only**\n\n   * Regex: `^[0-9]+$`\n\n2. **Alphanumeric or symbolic**\n\n   * Contains at least one letter or non-digit symbol\n   * Examples: `CPQ-123`, `Q-45`, `abc123`, `X_2024`\n\n---\n\n## EXTRACTION RULES (EXECUTED IN ORDER)\n\n1. Scan `inputMessage`.\n2. Tokenize by whitespace.\n3. Remove tokens that are:\n   * Common verbs or filler words:\n``` accept, approve, reject, cancel, submit,get, fetch, show, tell, give,what,when,who,how, is, the, of, for, to, in,status, details, information,this, that, current, latest, my,quote, quotes, please,modify, inquire,about,more,ask,details,modified,expiry,modification, modifications,update, updated, updates, updating,change, changed, changes, changing,edit, edited, edits, editing,check,last, date, time```\n   * Pure punctuation or symbols with no alphanumeric characters.\n4. From the remaining tokens:\n   * Keep only tokens that contain **at least one alphanumeric character**.\n   * Trim leading and trailing punctuation.\n5. If **multiple candidate tokens remain**:\n   * Select the **single longest token**.\n6. If **no valid token remains**:\n   * Treat the identifier as missing.\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT — JSON ONLY)\n\n```\n{\n  \"quoteId\": \"string or null\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT RULES (ENFORCED)\n\n* Return **only** the extracted identifier string or `null`.\n* Do **not** classify the identifier.\n* Do **not** infer intent.\n* Do **not** resolve from history.\n* Never return filler words or descriptive terms.\n* Never return partial JSON.\n\n---\n\n## GUARANTEES (MUST HOLD)\n\n* “Accept this quote” → `null`\n* “Get details of current quote” → `null`\n* “What are the products in my latest quote” → `null`\n* “Accept quote CPQ-123” → `\"CPQ-123\"`\n* “Accept quote 300000010424227” → `\"300000010424227\"`\n* “Accept quote 343” → `\"343\"`\n\nThis node exists **only** to answer:\n\n> “Did the user explicitly type an identifier?”"
            },
            {
              "id": "1762931732634_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"quoteId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
