            "sourceCode": "var quoteId = $context.$nodes.GET_TRANSACTION_ID.$output?.[0]?.text;\n\nvar userInputQuoteId = $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_QUOTE_IDENTIFIER.$output;\n\nvar isQuoteIdEmpty = (quoteId == null || quoteId === \"\");\nvar isUserInputEmpty = (userInputQuoteId == null || userInputQuoteId === \"\");\n\nreturn (isQuoteIdEmpty && isUserInputEmpty);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768317971015"
          },
          "code": "QUOTE_ID_VALIDATOR",
          "id": "1768319220150",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Quote Identifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768319220150"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_QUOTE_IDENTIFIER",
          "id": "1768320348573",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768320348574_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### SYSTEM INSTRUCTION\n\nYou are an AI responsible for extracting an explicit quote identifier from a user input message.\n\nThis node performs strict extraction only.\nIt must never infer, never resolve from history, and never use semantics beyond basic filtering.\nIf the user does not explicitly type a quote identifier, return null.\n\nOutput only a single raw value:\n- the extracted identifier string\n- or the literal null\n\nDo not output JSON.\nDo not include explanations, commentary, or prose.\nDo not wrap the output in quotes.\n\n---\n\n## INPUT\n\ninputMessage: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n---\n\n## EXTRACTION SCOPE (HARD BOUNDARY)\n\nExtract an identifier only if it is explicitly present in the text.\n\nThe following do not qualify as explicit identifiers and must return null:\n- this quote\n- that quote\n- current quote\n- latest quote\n- my quote\n- any reference requiring chat history\n\n---\n\n## IDENTIFIER DEFINITION (AUTHORITATIVE)\n\nA valid explicit quote identifier is a single token that is either:\n\n1. Digits-only\n   - Regex: ^[0-9]+$\n\n2. Alphanumeric or symbolic\n   - Contains at least one letter or non-digit symbol\n   - Examples: CPQ-123, Q-45, abc123, X_2024\n\n---\n\n## EXTRACTION RULES (EXECUTED IN ORDER)\n\n1. Scan inputMessage.\n2. Tokenize by whitespace.\n3. Remove tokens that are:\n   - Common verbs or filler words:\n     accept, approve, reject, cancel, submit, get, fetch, show, tell, give,\n     what, when, who, how, is, the, of, for, to, in, status, details,\n     information, this, that, current, latest, my, quote, quotes, please,\n     modify, inquire, about, more, ask, modified, expiry, modification,\n     modifications, update, updated, updates, updating, change, changed,\n     changes, changing, edit, edited, edits, editing, check, last, date, time,\n     request, requests,changes, on, update\n   - Pure punctuation or symbols with no alphanumeric characters\n4. From the remaining tokens:\n   - Trim leading and trailing punctuation\n   - Keep only tokens that contain at least one alphanumeric character\n5. Identify candidate tokens that match the identifier definition:\n   - digits-only, or\n   - alphanumeric/symbolic tokens that contain at least one letter, or\n   - alphanumeric/symbolic tokens that contain at least one digit\n6. If multiple candidate tokens remain, return the first candidate token that matches the identifier definition exactly.\n7. If no valid token remains, return null.\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT RULES (ENFORCED)\n\n- Return only the extracted identifier string or null.\n- Do not classify the identifier.\n- Do not infer intent.\n- Do not resolve from history.\n- Never return filler words or descriptive terms.\n- Never return partial JSON.\n\n---\n\n## GUARANTEES (MUST HOLD)\n\n- “Accept this quote” → null\n- “Get details of current quote” → null\n- “What are the products in my latest quote” → null\n- “Accept quote CPQ-123” → CPQ-123\n- “Accept quote 300000010424227” → 300000010424227\n- “Accept quote 343” → 343\n\nThis node exists only to answer:\n\n“Did the user explicitly type an identifier?”"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Quote ID Parser",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var quoteId = $context.$nodes.GET_TRANSACTION_ID.$output?.[0]?.text;\nvar userInputQuoteId = $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_QUOTE_IDENTIFIER.$output;\n\nlet output = { value: \"\",  identifierType:\"\" };\n\n// Pick the first non-empty value\nvar finalIdRaw = (quoteId != null && quoteId !== \"\") ? quoteId : userInputQuoteId;\nvar finalId = finalIdRaw != null ? String(finalIdRaw).trim() : \"\";\n\n// Determine the identifier type\nvar identifierType;\n\n// Check if finalId is purely numeric\nif (finalId != null && /^[0-9]+$/.test(finalId)) {\n  identifierType = \"TransactionIdentifier\";\n} else {\n  identifierType = \"QuoteIdentifier\";\n}\n\noutput.value=finalId;\noutput.identifierType=identifierType;\nreturn output;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768324784586"
          },
          "code": "QUOTE_ID_PARSER",
          "id": "1768321080854",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
