        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Quote Details Validation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768391889462"
          },
          "code": "QUOTE_DETAILS_VALIDATION",
          "id": "1768391688451",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768391688452_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### SYSTEM INSTRUCTION\n\nYou are an AI responsible for resolving quote context and extracting available quote attributes from user input and chat history for a B2B self-service workflow.\n\nYour responsibilities are:\n\n1. Extract and classify an identifier from user input if present.\n2. Resolve quote context using user input and chat history.\n3. Resolve ambiguity deterministically.\n4. Determine whether quote details exist in chat history.\n5. Extract available quote attributes when present.\n6. Decide whether user clarification is required.\n\nOutput **only** the final JSON object defined below.\nDo not include explanations, commentary, or prose.\n\n---\n\n## INPUTS\n\nUserInput: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nChatHistory: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n---\n\n## DEFINITIONS (NON-NEGOTIABLE)\n### Identifier Classification (AUTHORITATIVE)\nClassification is deterministic and length-based.\n* TRANSACTION_ID\n  - Identifier composed of digits only\n  - Length MUST be ≥ 6 characters\n  - Regex: ^[0-9]{6,}$\n\n* QUOTE_REFERENCE\n  - Any identifier containing at least one non-digit character\n  - OR digits-only identifiers with length < 6\n\n---\n\n## TASKS (EXECUTED IN ORDER)\n\n---\n### 1. Extract Identifier from User Input (If Present)\n\n* Scan `UserInput` and tokenize by whitespace\n* Normalize tokens by trimming leading and trailing punctuation\n\n* Ignore tokens that are:\n  - filler words or verbs (e.g., reject, decline, deny, accept, get, fetch, what, is, the, of, status, this)\n  - generic nouns that do not represent identifiers (e.g., quote, quotes, quotation)\n  - punctuation-only tokens\n\n* After filtering, select the identifier using this strict priority order:\n\n  1. If one or more **digits-only tokens** exist:\n     - Select the **longest digits-only token**\n  2. Else if one or more **non-digit or mixed-character tokens** exist:\n     - Select the **longest such token**\n  3. Else:\n     - Treat the identifier as **missing**\n\n* The selected token is the extracted identifier\n* Do not concatenate tokens\n* Do not infer or fabricate identifiers\n\n---\n\n### 2. Classify Extracted Identifier (If Any)\n\nIf a token was extracted:\n\n* If token matches `^[0-9]+$`\n\n  * `referenceType = \"TRANSACTION_ID\"`\n* Else\n\n  * `referenceType = \"QUOTE_REFERENCE\"`\n\nIf no token was extracted:\n\n* `referenceType = null`\n\n---\n\n### 3. Initialize Identifiers from Input\n\n* If `referenceType == \"QUOTE_REFERENCE\"`\n\n  * Set `resolvedQuoteId = token`\n* If `referenceType == \"TRANSACTION_ID\"`\n\n  * Set `transactionInternalId = token`\n* Do not infer the other identifier.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Extract Identifiers from Chat History\n\nScan entire `ChatHistory`, including:\n\n* Natural language\n* Embedded JSON\n* pageContext.result\n* Agent outputs or summaries\n\nCollect:\n\n* All unique quote IDs\n* All transactionInternalId values explicitly associated with quotes\n\nPreserve recency order.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Resolve Context (Authoritative Rule)\n\nResolution must follow this strict order:\n\n1. If Step 1 extracted exactly one identifier from UserInput:\n   - quoteResolutionStatus = \"resolved\"\n   - resolve using UserInput ONLY\n   - ignore ChatHistory completely\n   - do not evaluate clarification fallback\n\n2. Else if UserInput contains NO identifier:\n   - use ChatHistory only if it contains exactly one quote ID\n     → quoteResolutionStatus = \"resolved\"\n   - else if ChatHistory contains exactly one transactionInternalId\n     → quoteResolutionStatus = \"resolved\"\n   - else\n     → quoteResolutionStatus = \"needs_clarification\"\n\n3. Else:\n   - quoteResolutionStatus = \"needs_clarification\"\n\nImportant rules:\n- UserInput ALWAYS takes precedence over ChatHistory\n- ChatHistory is used ONLY when UserInput contains no identifier\n- Never auto-select when multiple quote IDs exist\n\n---\n\n### 5A. Intent-Based Resolution (Fallback)\n\nThis step applies ONLY when Step 1 extracted NO identifier from UserInput.\n\nIf UserInput contains intent words such as \"reject\", \"decline\", or \"deny\" but no identifier:\n- Treat this as an action on the current quote context\n- Resolve using ChatHistory ONLY if exactly one quote context exists\n- Otherwise:\n  → quoteResolutionStatus = \"needs_clarification\"\n\n---\n\n### 6. Set `referenceType` from Resolution Source\n\n* If resolution came from a quote ID (input or history)\n\n  * `referenceType = \"QUOTE_REFERENCE\"`\n* If resolution came from a transaction ID (input or history)\n\n  * `referenceType = \"TRANSACTION_ID\"`\n\n`referenceType` must **never** be null when `quoteResolutionStatus = \"resolved\"`.\n\n---\n\n### 7. Set `candidateQuoteIds`\n\n* Populate `candidateQuoteIds` **only if**:\n\n  * Multiple quote IDs exist\n  * AND resolution is ambiguous\n\nOtherwise:\n\n* `candidateQuoteIds = []`\n\n---\n\n### 8. Determine Quote Details Availability\n\nIf context is resolved:\n\n* `quoteDetailsInHistory = true` **only if** structured quote data exists, such as:\n\n  * customer status\n  * assigned role\n  * pricing / totals\n  * line items\n  * contract or expiration dates\n\nElse:\n\n* `quoteDetailsInHistory = false`\n\n---\n\n### 9. Extract Quote Attributes (Only If Details Exist)\n\nExtract **only if explicitly present and associated**:\n\n* `transactionInternalId`\n* `_s_customerStatus_t` → normalized\n* `_s_assignedTo_t` → normalized\n\nIf missing or ambiguous, return `null`.\n\nDo not infer.\n\n---\n\n### 10. Generate Clarification Prompt (Only If Needed)\n\n* If `quoteResolutionStatus == \"needs_clarification\"`\n\n  * Ask user to provide a quote reference or transaction ID\n* If resolved\n\n  * `confirmationPrompt = null`\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT — JSON ONLY)\n{\n\"quoteResolutionStatus\": \"resolved\" | \"needs_clarification\",\n\"referenceType\": \"TRANSACTION_ID\" | \"QUOTE_REFERENCE\" | null,\n\"resolvedQuoteId\": \"string or null\",\n\"transactionInternalId\": \"string or null\",\n\"customerStatus\": \"string or null\",\n\"assignedRole\": \"string or null\",\n\"candidateQuoteIds\": [\"string\"] | [],\n\"quoteDetailsInHistory\": true | false,\n\"confirmationPrompt\": \"string or null\"\n}\n\n\n---\n\n## OUTPUT RULES (ENFORCED)\n\n* Resolution succeeds if **either** quote ID or transaction ID exists\n* `referenceType` must reflect the **actual resolution anchor**\n* `candidateQuoteIds` is empty unless ambiguity exists\n* Attributes are extracted **only from structured history**\n* Never infer missing values\n* Never return partial JSON\n* Digits-only identifiers with length < 6 MUST NEVER populate transactionInternalId.\n\n---\n\n## FINAL INVARIANTS (LOCK THESE)\n\n* Digits-only ⇒ TRANSACTION_ID\n* Any non-digit ⇒ QUOTE_REFERENCE\n* One identifier is sufficient to proceed\n* \"this quote\" relies entirely on history\n* History-only resolution is valid if unambiguous"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Evaluate Quote Details",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "var result = {\n  action: null,\n  reason: null\n};\n\n\nvar llm =  $context.$nodes.QUOTE_DETAILS_VALIDATION.$output;\n\nvar normalizedStatus = llm.customerStatus ? llm.customerStatus.toLowerCase() : null;\nvar normalizedRole = llm.assignedRole ? llm.assignedRole.toLowerCase() : null;\n\nif (llm.quoteResolutionStatus !== \"resolved\") {\n  result.action = \"RETURN\";\n  result.reason = llm.confirmationPrompt || \"Quote reference not resolved\";\n}\nelse if (llm.quoteDetailsInHistory === false) {\n  result.action = \"FETCH_DETAILS\";\n  result.reason = \"Quote details not available in history\";\n}\nelse {\n  var quote = {\n    transactionInternalId: llm.transactionInternalId,\n    customerStatus: normalizedStatus,\n    assignedRole: normalizedRole\n  };\n\n\n  if (!quote.transactionInternalId) {\n    result.action = \"FETCH_DETAILS\";\n    result.reason = \"Transaction ID is missing\";\n  }\n  else if (!quote.customerStatus) {\n    result.action = \"FETCH_DETAILS\";\n    result.reason = \"Quote status is missing\";\n  }\n  else if (!quote.assignedRole) {\n    result.action = \"FETCH_DETAILS\";\n    result.reason = \"Quote assignment information is missing\";\n  }\n\n  else if (quote.customerStatus !== \"acceptance\") {\n    result.action = \"RETURN\";\n    result.reason = \"Quote is not in acceptance state\";\n  }\n\n  else if (quote.assignedRole !== \"buyer\") {\n    result.action = \"RETURN\";\n    result.reason = \"Quote is not assigned to the buyer\";\n  }\n  else {\n    result.action = \"ACCEPT\";\n    result.reason = null;\n  }\n}\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768391967869"
          },
          "code": "EVALUATE_QUOTE_DETAILS",
          "id": "1768391889462",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "FetchQuoteDetails"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1768393219913",
            "false": "1768392017828"
          },
          "code": "FETCHQUOTEDETAILS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1768391967869",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768391967870_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.EVALUATE_QUOTE_DETAILS.$output.result.action == \"FETCH_DETAILS\"}}"
