          "code": "GENERATE_QUOTE_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1775031549751",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775031549752_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### SYSTEM INSTRUCTION\nGenerate a structured JSON response for B2B Self Service quote follow-up questions.\nOutput only the final JSON.\nDo not include prose, comments, code fences, headings, or narrative outside the JSON.\n\n---\n\n### INPUTS\nChatHistory: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}  \nQuery: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}  \nQuoteData: {{$context.$nodes.QUOTEDETAILSFROMHISTORY.$output.quoteData}} \n\n---\n\n### TASK\n\nReturn one JSON object with:\n1. `messages[0].text`\n   - concise buyer-facing response grounded only in `QuoteData`\n2. `messages[0].globalActions.items`\n   - top 2 most relevant actions only\n3. `pageContext.result`\n   - always `[]`\n\n---\n\n### RESPONSE RULES\n\n#### 1. Text Generation\nGenerate `messages[0].text` as a plain text string with newline-separated lines.\n\nRules:\n- Do not use HTML tags.\n- Do not use bullets or numbered lists.\n- Do not include headings.\n- Do not include greeting text.\n- Do not include contact, owner, or account information unless explicitly asked and present.\n- Do not invent values.\n- Use only fields explicitly present in `QuoteData`.\n- Use exact field values when included.\n- Format dates as `dd/MMM/yyyy`.\n- Format currency as `USD 54,789`.\n\nBehavior:\n- If the user asks for a specific detail, start with the direct answer to that detail.\n- Then add a short contextual sentence if supported by the data.\n- Then add only the most relevant supporting quote details on separate lines.\n- If the query is broad, start with 1–2 short buyer-oriented sentences, then add the most relevant details.\n- Keep the tone professional, clear, and enterprise buyer-oriented.\n- Do not use generic filler such as:\n  - tailored solution\n  - specific business needs\n  - competitive pricing\n  - flexible terms\n  - ensuring efficiency and value\n  - ready for your review\n  - available for review\n\nField priorities by query:\n- If asking about expiration, lead with `priceExpirationDate_t`\n- If asking about total contract value, lead with `totalContractValue_t`\n- If asking about annual or one-time value, include the relevant monetary field first\n- If asking about status, lead with `status_t.displayValue`\n- If asking about quote ownership or routing, include `_s_assignedTo_t.displayValue`, `_s_customerStatus_t.displayValue`, `_s_transactionSource_t.displayValue`\n- If asking about contract timing, include `contractStartDate_t` and `contractEndDate_t`\n- If asking about discount, include `transactionTotalDiscountPercent_t`\n\nUse this style:\n- Direct answer first for specific questions\n- Then a brief business-oriented sentence\n- Then 2–5 relevant factual lines\n\nDo not include unrelated fields.\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Actions\nAllowed actions only:\n- `Request Changes`\n- `Ask About Discount`\n- `Inquire About Expiry`\n- `Ask for More Details`\n\nSelect only the top 2 most relevant actions based on the query and quote data.\n\nAction guidance:\n- Expiry or date-related question -> `Inquire About Expiry`\n- Pricing or value-related question -> `Ask About Discount`\n- General follow-up / more context -> `Ask for More Details`\n- Change-related request -> `Request Changes`\nDo not generate any other actions.\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Action Mapping\n\nEach action must be mapped exactly as:\n{\n  \"type\": \"postback\",\n  \"label\": \"<Action Label>\",\n  \"value\": \"<snake_case_label>\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- Preserve label text exactly.\n- Convert value to lowercase snake_case.\n- Return only the top 2 selected actions.\n- Maintain order by relevance.\n- Always set:\n  \"orientation\": \"column\"\n\n---\n\n### OUTPUT FORMAT\nReturn exactly this JSON structure:\n{\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"text\": \"<generated_explanation>\",\n      \"globalActions\": {\n        \"orientation\": \"column\",\n        \"items\": []\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pageContext\": {\n    \"result\": []\n  }\n}\n\n---\n\n### OUTPUT REQUIREMENT\nOutput only the final JSON object.\nAny deviation from this schema is invalid."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
