              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "QuoteListing Response Summarizer"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775041218003"
          },
          "code": "QUOTELISTING_RESPONSE_SUMMARIZER",
          "id": "1775040963193",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775040963193_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### SYSTEM INSTRUCTION\nGenerate a structured JSON response for B2B Self Service quote list / quote filter queries.\nOutput only the final JSON.\nDo not include prose, comments, code fences, headings, or narrative outside the JSON.\n\n---\n\n### INPUTS\n\nQuery: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nQuoteDetails: {{$context.$nodes.CLEAN_QUOTE_DATA.$output.result}} \n\n---\n\n### TASK OVERVIEW\n\n1. Generate a **concise, buyer-centric quote summary** in **HTML** format that directly answers the query.\n   - Present the quote as a **virtual sales rep** would, in a friendly, professional, enterprise tone.\n   - **Do not include system-style status statements**.\n   - **Do not include \"Next suggested steps\"** or explicit instructions.\n   - **Do not include contact, owner, or account information** anywhere in the summary.\n   - **No headings** like \"Quote\", \"Summary\", or \"Value to Buyer.\"\n   - **No dates in the opening paragraph.** If dates appear in highlights, format as **dd/MMM/yyyy**.\n   - For list/filter queries, enumerate each matching quote separately.\n   - Do not return narrative-only summaries.\n   - Do not return aggregated or analytical summaries such as counts-only, totals-only, or generic rollups.\n   - When multiple quotes match, each quote must be represented separately in the explanation.\n   - For broad list/filter queries, start with a short paragraph summarizing the matching set naturally, then provide quote-level highlights.\n   - Do not highlight any monetary attribute that is zero dollar.\n   - Omit any missing fields.\n   - Tone: professional, clear, persuasive, friendly.\n   - For specific attribute questions such as expiry, last modified date, status, product count, or line item count:\n     - return only the requested information\n     - do not include the summary paragraph\n     - do not include unrelated highlights\n\n2. `messages[0].globalActions.items` must always contain these 3 actions:\n   - View Quote\n   - Accept Quote\n   - Request Changes\n\n3. Do not generate `pageContext.result` in this prompt. That will be handled later in code.\n\n4. Output only the final JSON in the required format.\n\n---\n\n### RULES\n\n#### Explanation Text (HTML, Buyer-Centric)\n\n* Quote Summary:\n  - For list/filter queries, provide a short buyer-friendly opening sentence followed by quote-level highlights.\n  - Use a list-style explanation when multiple quotes are present.\n  - Do not collapse multiple quotes into a single narrative.\n  - Do not summarize across quotes.\n  - Do not use generic filler phrases such as:\n    - tailored solution\n    - specific business needs\n    - competitive pricing\n    - flexible terms\n    - ensuring efficiency and value\n    - ready for your review\n    - available for review\n  - Include only values explicitly present in `QuoteDetails`.\n  - Do not paraphrase field values.\n  - Do not invent missing values.\n  - Do not include attributes that are not relevant to the query.\n\n* Field grounding guidance:\n  - Prefer using `transactionName` naturally in the opening summary when available.\n  - Use values from fields such as status, transaction source, customer status, assignment, contract dates, expiry, and monetary fields when they are relevant to the query.\n  - Always use field values exactly as provided when included.\n\n* Highlight selection logic:\n  - If the query asks about status, include status-related fields first.\n  - If the query asks about dates or expiry, include date-related fields first.\n  - If the query asks about pricing or contract value, include pricing-related fields first.\n  - If the query asks about participants or ownership, include assigned/customer/source fields first.\n  - If the query is general, choose the most commercially relevant attributes from the available data.\n  - If the query is a filter such as:\n    - rejected quotes\n    - expiring quotes\n    - quotes above a value threshold\n    - quotes with specific status\n    then the explanation should emphasize the matching attribute first.\n\n* Date formatting:\n  - Use `dd/MMM/yyyy`\n\n* Specific attribute questions:\n  - If the query asks only for one attribute, return only that value as a direct factual response.\n  - Do not include the general summary or additional highlights.\n\n* Use only values explicitly present in `QuoteDetails`.\n* Escape double quotes properly.\n\n---\n\n#### Global Actions\n\n* `messages[0].globalActions.orientation` must always be `\"column\"`.\n* `messages[0].globalActions.items` must always contain exactly these 3 postback actions in this order:\n  1. View Quote\n  2. Accept Quote\n  3. Request Changes\n\n---\n\n#### Action Mapping Rules\n\nEach action string must be converted to:\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"postback\",\n  \"label\": \"<Action Label>\",\n  \"value\": \"<snake_case_label>\"\n}\n\n* Preserve label text exactly.\n* Convert value to lowercase snake_case.\n* Maintain the order defined above.\n\n---\n\n#### Final Output Format (STRICT — SINGLE JSON ONLY)\n\n{\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"text\": <generated_explanation>,\n      \"globalActions\": {\n        \"orientation\": \"column\",\n        \"items\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"postback\",\n            \"label\": \"View Quote\",\n            \"value\": \"view_quote\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"postback\",\n            \"label\": \"Accept Quote\",\n            \"value\": \"accept_quote\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"postback\",\n            \"label\": \"Request Changes\",\n            \"value\": \"request_changes\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n* Always return `\"orientation\": \"column\"`.\n* Do not include any other fields.\n\n---\n\n### OUTPUT REQUIREMENT\n\nOutput only the final JSON object described above.\nAny deviation from this schema is invalid."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "QuoteListingResponse",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const messageData = $context.$nodes.QUOTELISTING_RESPONSE_SUMMARIZER.$output;\nconst pageContextData = $context.$nodes.CLEAN_QUOTE_DATA.$output;\n\nconst outputMessage =\n  messageData &&\n  Array.isArray(messageData.messages) &&\n  messageData.messages.length > 0\n    ? messageData.messages[0]\n    : {};\n\nlet result = [];\n\nif (pageContextData && pageContextData.result) {\n  if (Array.isArray(pageContextData.result.items)) {\n    result = pageContextData.result.items;\n  } else if (Array.isArray(pageContextData.result)) {\n    result = pageContextData.result;\n  } else if (typeof pageContextData.result === \"object\") {\n    result = [pageContextData.result];\n  }\n}\n\nreturn {\n  messages: [\n    {\n      type: \"text\",\n      text: outputMessage.text || \"\",\n      globalActions: {\n        orientation: \"column\",\n        items: []\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  pageContext: {\n    result: result\n  }\n};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775041910539"
          },
