        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "extractQuoteDetailsByTransaction"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1764150711754"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACTQUOTEDETAILSBYTRANSACTION",
          "id": "1776271251219",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776271251219_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Respond to: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nUse quote details only from: {{$context.$variables.quoteDetails}}\nSubscriptionReference: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_AND_RETURN_SUBSCRIPTIONID.$output.result}}\n\nReturn only fields that are relevant to the user’s query.\n\nAlways include these fields when relevant:\n`totalOneTimeNetAmount_t`, `totalContractValue_t`, `_date_modified`, `_s_customerStatus_t`, `_s_assignedTo_t`, `lastupdatedDate_t`, `_last_modified_date`\n\nInclude `transactionLines` only when directly needed to answer the query.\n\nSubscription rules:\n- For subscription details tied to the quote, use `SubscriptionReference` as the only valid subscription identifier.\n- Do not derive subscription information from `transactionLines`, product type, rate plans, recurring revenue, or any other quote field.\n- If `SubscriptionReference` is null or empty, say no subscription reference is available for the quote.\n- Do not use `renewDraftSubscriptionNumber_t` directly from `quoteDetails` when `SubscriptionReference` is present.\n\nGeneral rules:\n- Use only values explicitly present in the quote details.\n- Do not infer, derive, or assume missing information.\n- Keep the response focused and relevant.\n- Do not include unrelated fields or excessive data.\n- Do not suggest actions.\n\nAlways include any links present in the quote details.\nRespond in natural language."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
